// The count of Process.err_read_bytes() must be an integer, and an integer is
// an Int or an integer-valued Number (spec/05-stdlib.md, Integer arguments).
// The child writes six bytes to its standard error, so the Int count reads the
// same two bytes. A fractional count is a runtime error that halts the
// program.
// COVERS: integer-arg process-err-read-bytes
// STATUS: error
// TIMEOUT: 30
// CHECK: ab
var p = spawn("/bin/sh", ["-c", "printf abcdef 1>&2"]);
print p.err_read_bytes(2i);
p.err_read_bytes(2.5);
print "unreachable";
